  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nNorthwest flow off of the lake will maintain lingering lake \nclouds through much of the day. A couple very light showers\ncannot be completely ruled out, but the vast majority of the\narea will remain dry. High pressure building eastward from the \nMidwest will begin to influence the region tonight, setting the \nstage for another extended stretch of dry weather. \n\nCool and dry conditions will persist into the weekend, with\nnorthwest flow continuing through Saturday. By Sunday an upper\nlevel ridge will begin building into the region from the west,\nallowing flow aloft to shift more westerly. This ridge will\nremain in place through the middle of next week, accompanied by\nsurface high pressure that will maintain the unusually dry\npattern. \n\nTemperatures will be coolest today and Saturday, with afternoon\nhighs ranging from the mid 50s to lower 60s. A gradual warming \ntrend will follow Sunday through the middle of next week with \nhighs climbing into the upper 50s to upper 60s. Some locations \nmay even approach 70 degrees at times next week. The next \nopportunity for more meaningful rainfall looks to arrive late \nWednesday into Thursday of next week.",
